From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sireesh Kodali <sireeshkodali1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 21:55:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] net: ipa: Add timeout for ipa_cmd_pipeline_clear_wait

Sometimes the pipeline clear fails, and when it does, having a hang in
kernel is ugly. The timeout gives us a nice error message. Note that
this shouldn't actually hang, ever. It only hangs if there is a mistake
in the config, and the timeout is only useful when debugging.

Signed-off-by: Vladimir Lypak <vladimir.lypak@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Sireesh Kodali <sireeshkodali1@gmail.com>
[psigod: port to 7.3: ipa->dev]
Signed-off-by: psigod <psigod@example.com>
---
 drivers/net/ipa/ipa_cmd.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_cmd.c b/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_cmd.c
index 984311a9a5..94bf290ce1 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_cmd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ipa/ipa_cmd.c
@@ -616,7 +616,10 @@ u32 ipa_cmd_pipeline_clear_count(void)
 
 void ipa_cmd_pipeline_clear_wait(struct ipa *ipa)
 {
-	wait_for_completion(&ipa->completion);
+	/* This only hangs if the pipeline clear is misconfigured */
+	if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&ipa->completion,
+					 msecs_to_jiffies(1000)))
+		dev_err(ipa->dev, "pipeline clear timed out\n");
 }
 
 /* Allocate a transaction for the command TX endpoint */
